Implementation notes mapping the reference to the scene:

- **Glowing double-rail guideway:** a `CatmullRomCurve3` is sampled and a `Frenet` frame basis is used to extrude two parallel `TubeGeometry` neon rails (cyan) plus a faint centre guide line and an additive halo tube — exactly the sweeping cyan "two-line" track that starts bottom-right and curves to the horizon in the screenshot. Glowing cross-ties and support pylons anchor it.
- **Monorail train:** a faceted body with conical nose/tail, an additive cyan cockpit window with a white core, side neon window strips, magenta underbody trim, amber top trim, a line-drawn **pantograph** diamond on top, and three rear **thruster torus rings** (cyan/amber) with exhaust glow sprites — echoing the ring motifs in the reference. The train is oriented per-frame using a re-orthogonalised tangent basis so it stays upright on the curve and animates along it.
- **City architecture:** procedurally generated `CanvasTexture` window grids used as emissive maps give towering skyscrapers volumetric lit-window patterns; magenta crown plates, neon `EdgesGeometry` trims, rooftop antennae with blinking tip sprites, and holographic billboard planes (custom canvas text + glitch bars) flank the corridor. The big **wireframe magenta orb with an orbit ring** is rebuilt as a holographic advertisement cluster. Scattered small neon rectangles, thin vertical light-beams, and floating torus "ring clusters" reproduce the floating signage and ground rings seen in the image.
- **Lighting & atmosphere:** near-black `FogExp2`, a cyan key `SpotLight`, magenta + amber `PointLight`s, and additive emissive materials produce the cinematic cyberpunk palette on a void background with a starfield/dust `Points` cloud. A metallic dark ground plane plus additive radial "puddle glow" planes fake the wet reflective surface.
- **Weather:** 1 400 vertical `LineSegments` rain streaks fall and wrap, triggering expanding **splash ring** sprites (cyan/magenta/amber) at the wet ground, while a CSS layer adds subtle diagonal screen rain-streaks, scanlines, vignette and grain.
- **Camera & interactivity:** `OrbitControls` with damping, slow auto-rotation, polar clamps, and a slow cinematic dolly of the orbit target toward the horizon centre to match the reference perspective.

All dependencies are loaded from the cdnjs r128 bundle (core + `OrbitControls`); textures are generated at runtime so the file is fully self-contained with no external assets or placeholders.
